rotocol_processor_top.sv` and `KL_aecp_notify.sv`. Two declare-before-use sites remain:\n- `KL_pp_originator.sv:194` `cancel_hit_w`\n- `KL_pp_rx_validator.sv:383` `vd_push_w`\n\n**Items:**\n1. **Check the patches first.** Before any edit, run `git grep -F` for every line you will move or change, across `tb/**/*.patch` and the exact-text mutant tables. If a patch carries one of those lines as context, refresh that context in the same commit. After the change, show that every mutation arm still plants.\n2. **Fix.** Move each declaration above its first use. This is a pure reordering: no logic, port, register or parameter change.\n3. **Prove no behaviour change.** The Yosys netlist statistics for both modules and for `protocol_processor_top` must be identical at base and head. Every processor suite record must be identical.\n4. **Prove zero declare-before-use.** Run `xvlog -sv` over every file in the processor's derived HDL source list. Report zero `VRFC 10-3380` and zero `VRFC 10-8530`, with the per-file table.\n   - xvlog is analysis only, so it may run without the Vivado lock.\n   - Do not run synthesis or implementation.\n5. **Parent ratchet.** The parent's `scripts/xvlog.budget` carries both sites (lines 34-35 at parent dev `28f9666f`). Write `parent-adoption-22-28f9666f.patch`, which drops those two lines. The parent consumer set must pass with it. The parent's `scripts/xvlog_gate.py --check` must pass in the scratch parent with your head and the patch.\n\n**STOP condition:** any change that is not a pure declaration move.\n\n**Gates:**\n- every processor suite;\n- `make check`, Yosys and lint;\n- the parent consumer set of 17 at parent dev `28f9666f`, with the 148 patch and your 22 patch, in that order.\n\n**Output:** HANDOFF.md and PR-BODY.md (\"Closes #22\" if every acceptance item is met). Then post REVIEW READY with the head on #22. Do not push.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"http